# Puca: nightly DB backup + 5-min health check  ->  /etc/cron.d/puca
#
# The scripts run as ROOT, so they live where only root can write:
# /usr/local/lib/puca-ops (see deploy/ops/README.md, Install). NOT in the
# install dir: /opt/puca belongs to the service user, and a root-run script
# in a directory someone else owns is theirs to replace.
#
# The scripts resolve their OWN names (/opt/puca or a pre-rename
# /opt/sovereign) and abort loudly (exit 78, which cron mails to you) rather
# than quietly back up or monitor nothing. See names.sh, which must sit beside
# them: they source it from their own directory.
#
# flock -n: a run that is still going when the next is due is left to finish,
# never doubled up.
0 3 * * * root flock -n /run/puca-backup.lock /usr/local/lib/puca-ops/backup.sh
*/5 * * * * root flock -n /run/puca-health.lock /usr/local/lib/puca-ops/healthcheck.sh
